  "code": "INELIG",
  "loc": "Abstract; Section II (Model)",
  "quote": "model of an interest group\u2019s strategic decision to publicly mobilize supportive voters",
  "note": "This is a signaling model of interest-group mobilization and a politician's policy choice. It does not study a voting rule that aggregates several agents' inputs into a collective decision. The election is a payoff device, and voters choose whether to join an event. This is political economy, not voting theory."
